Package: bsh-shell
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: bsh
Provides: bsh
Replaces: bsh
Description: High-performance spacetime-aware custom shell (BrightShell)
 Bsh (BrightShell) is an interactive shell derived from zsh, extended with
 BrightDate (a timezone-free SI-day timestamp system), AI-assisted
 completions, and other enhancements suited for modern development workflows.
 .
 BrightDate replaces timezone-aware timestamps with a single floating-point
 SI-day count since J2000.0, making log correlation and time arithmetic
 trivially correct across machines and timezones.
 .
 Note: This package replaces the legacy Java BeanShell (bsh) package.
